course: dictionary
lesson: 6027
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Meeting is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Before a trip, a family can agree on a meeting place in case someone gets separated.» Here meeting place is the spot where people agree to go, so they can find each other.
explain: «The class had a meeting about the school trip.» Here meeting means people coming together to talk, plan or decide. The clues are class and school trip. Check by swapping in another word: "The class had a talk about the school trip" still makes sense.
explain: Meeting can also mean the moment people meet, as in «our first meeting». Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then try each meaning in the sentence. The one that fits is the right one.
fact: Meeting is a noun (a meeting, meetings) and also the -ing form of the verb meet.
fact: «Meeting» means people coming together to talk about something, plan or decide.
fact: «Meeting place» means a spot people agree to go to, so they can find each other.
fact: «Meeting» can also mean a sports event, such as «an athletics meeting» (UK).
fact: Safety tip: agree a meeting point before you go out, in case you get lost.
exercise: «Before a trip, a family can agree on a meeting place in case someone gets separated.» What is a meeting place? | A place where you must sit very still | *A place people agree to go to so they can find each other | A kind of trip | A school bell
exercise: «Our first meeting was at the park, and we talked for hours.» What does meeting mean here? | *The moment people meet | A sports event | Playing a game with a ball | A plan for a school trip
exercise: «An appraisal is a meeting where a boss talks through how someone has done over the year.» What is the meeting for? | *To talk through how someone has done, like a grown-up school report | A picnic in the park | Learning to swim | Buying a new car
test: «The parents' meeting is on Thursday at six.» What kind of meeting is this? | *People coming together to talk about school | Lost in a crowd | A sports race | A kind of cake
test: Which word is the -ing form of the verb meet? | met | *meeting | meet | meets
exam: In «an athletics meeting», what kind of meeting is it? | A school lesson | *A sports event | A meeting of a club to plan a trip | Two friends having tea
